#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/id #uuid "e95210c5-adb4-519e-bbec-e240dac32fd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3614" :question/problem "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/id #uuid "b03496ac-c3b2-5d65-a3e3-2a33ea0cb862" :question/math-academy-id "e-3619" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{25}^{∘}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{25}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡{25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by $\\dfrac 1 2$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)} } = 3 \\left( \\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4483a191-ab5f-53cc-9a25-631101495ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256212} {:answer/id #uuid "1bca9c9f-347e-50cd-983a-012520b04ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256213} {:answer/id #uuid "7182fa70-cf00-5a72-8698-deb11fabc8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256214} {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} {:answer/id #uuid "4b12d860-258e-5359-827c-56ef56e1e69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4715576-2b79-520b-9527-45c19ddc2f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9834bdc8-d968-5825-adae-a20e0fb4ec63" :question/math-academy-id "q-119948" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f9fa087f-f6db-5d41-bce6-176e0dfc84bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265643} {:answer/id #uuid "8291aef2-a55a-5035-960c-b2fd32db51b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265644} {:answer/id #uuid "74e0f6fd-d7a9-5e32-b935-3d2d63d15eee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265645} {:answer/id #uuid "16abd149-1622-5870-acac-08550572af4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265646} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d7a1573-25a2-57b7-9e53-7a5153bbcccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265647} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e71bada-abf2-5012-a4dd-26de4973c091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d2067af-e1b2-5f04-ba26-5b2307cb8aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-120017" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "299a4036-7401-5ec0-be7f-2022c81d1096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281684} {:answer/id #uuid "5e74f45f-6145-5c80-9cfe-c0ed118e55bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} {:answer/id #uuid "9d36f77e-f34f-5865-a379-4b6195857bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281686} {:answer/id #uuid "023f9a63-2f22-5145-94fb-5736a13bae5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281687} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cb1f7d-bc36-5ff9-a3ee-57d48f84ac6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e74f45f-6145-5c80-9cfe-c0ed118e55bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281685} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac5edacb-bfbd-58aa-8234-65a8e4b4cad7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "178fb81d-b009-5067-9e70-c3ccaf69f0be" :question/math-academy-id "q-120029" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={50}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {50}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({100}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}=1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186257401 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baab2cc7-b73f-581a-b668-78f06150370b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298074} {:answer/id #uuid "917951ed-fcaa-5490-b660-b37efd0444ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298075} {:answer/id #uuid "87b71c19-e177-51d2-93c0-34a482735607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298076} {:answer/id #uuid "573d2542-2975-52b9-b5df-c9b4369ded5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298077} {:answer/id #uuid "cc13ce49-e4c1-5c0c-b988-f3175da14342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "573d2542-2975-52b9-b5df-c9b4369ded5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298077} :answer-field/id #uuid "c565bec4-62af-5e9a-b162-88142c03255b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72bde4a1-d04b-50b4-bd0e-183a00744709" :question/math-academy-id "q-120087" :question/problem "$10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed202dc5-ee81-586d-86e5-9ab11f560c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281691} {:answer/id #uuid "28acbdae-db5d-555e-9992-ecf841025666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281692} {:answer/id #uuid "397beb83-55b4-5c02-b7ad-41cdd0598e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281693} {:answer/id #uuid "66ebe9bc-0c6a-5192-a142-6bafb0f428aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281694} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d2ba0-9102-545b-b898-0f3bfdac943f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "397beb83-55b4-5c02-b7ad-41cdd0598e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281693} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe430471-858f-5d77-bff2-394ae8b417ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4169dfb7-ab66-5202-bba3-44ee807d3294" :question/math-academy-id "q-120088" :question/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ac8d37f-1f11-5095-87c7-37fd160497dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin (\\frac{π}{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057976} {:answer/id #uuid "a1588093-ba65-5916-bb3c-2f29b1c5132c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\csc (\\frac{π}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057977} {:answer/id #uuid "e83cf983-3776-580d-9330-551565c59025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec (\\frac{π}{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057978} {:answer/id #uuid "44e9a9d6-83a4-56d7-940a-a11d0ff920d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sec (\\frac{π}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057979} {:answer/id #uuid "49c49e45-81e4-5826-9f98-b6119943ce0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44e9a9d6-83a4-56d7-940a-a11d0ff920d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sec (\\frac{π}{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057979} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2dde19-cc77-5d77-ae13-89f8ae47d9cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2050e06-0476-56c1-a7a1-1d0ef234a4b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24642" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}}{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4bffe8b-3637-547c-99be-c2ee069ca61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256254} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b9e4e0-fa4d-5e47-b517-e31db15c125f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256255} {:answer/id #uuid "ed742626-ab3e-5908-9345-2200a481d3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} {:answer/id #uuid "0446b95c-c2af-560d-abd1-109cb4fc118a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bb793c7-2ed0-5340-b770-f69725fc53fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256253}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04ad99db-b562-50ab-884b-fce6f7ff1c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-24647" :question/problem "Express $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2c30caa-ff10-53b7-8fdd-aaf6f63bd0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298081} {:answer/id #uuid "09620807-7fce-52f8-bf4c-775e9549662b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298082} {:answer/id #uuid "b70159ab-5d3a-5bf3-8c8f-7eaf39e2cea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298083} {:answer/id #uuid "42cb2a7c-a995-5499-9701-3347f8f58a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298084} {:answer/id #uuid "3ada3d25-7168-56a9-acce-36cef20c5b52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c30caa-ff10-53b7-8fdd-aaf6f63bd0cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298081} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb925e20-c96e-5be1-8f73-b15a5af78f02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "234c5140-a4ed-5ffc-884a-a3cb29eba9e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-24781" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d272422f-c611-50b9-9fa7-b922724373dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058019} {:answer/id #uuid "4d587fd7-f6e3-56e2-972b-fe458491c52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058020} {:answer/id #uuid "51a38727-e193-5683-b295-c5726aadbee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058021} {:answer/id #uuid "5792f565-5923-5b00-89c8-34edc6cf5dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058022} {:answer/id #uuid "6910ae72-ad52-56f9-9a28-a78eb163a5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6910ae72-ad52-56f9-9a28-a78eb163a5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058023} :answer-field/id #uuid "c97ec4fe-dd15-55b5-b784-78de356f1b48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f5ad5b9-cf75-5c20-a9c5-6e5d15578fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24788" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})]-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =1-(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} {:answer/id #uuid "75fef84a-4659-5182-9dc8-65882bb13b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b960d8-b823-521f-ba0a-f080d7d65c62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "62770764-8176-56e9-8c60-1a1dcb94a9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-327716" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279} {:answer/id #uuid "88fa1ab4-35d1-5314-8020-820dde48504f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279} :answer-field/id #uuid "341f39aa-6a81-5083-8264-e503b649bf89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256278}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c3ab403-d373-50aa-ab7d-cad9629d8aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-327763" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd9685f1-7011-5e7c-ad95-1d98e4e0e37d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298089} {:answer/id #uuid "5310f57c-7f95-566e-ab96-bfd3321a80cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd9685f1-7011-5e7c-ad95-1d98e4e0e37d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298089} :answer-field/id #uuid "39225043-f2d9-5a43-af04-a30bed00f209" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7df0fa64-e505-5b6a-8722-426dd8a2b855" :question/math-academy-id "q-328087" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{24})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298091 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c6dabfd-9272-5b92-8b93-6ffc7a94f8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298093} {:answer/id #uuid "049d84c3-5dcd-51a6-a89d-941c6562271d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298094} {:answer/id #uuid "6d406fed-1761-56b4-96e4-a7031536d84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298095} {:answer/id #uuid "62113e5f-6e48-5729-83fd-962eab093710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298096} {:answer/id #uuid "fb006d59-2de8-558a-b0c3-d07648440291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c6dabfd-9272-5b92-8b93-6ffc7a94f8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298093} :answer-field/id #uuid "f59a9310-1cc1-5e1c-95eb-129665fa94a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298092}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6936b757-bb9a-5d9f-83d7-ff21b4bd2dc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-65612" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={24}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {24}^{∘})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}}{\\cancel{2}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4eb6d0c-2996-52f5-a261-6c1ef2915eca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298100} {:answer/id #uuid "a9330c30-7093-5ea5-ae50-c2e0f22d89fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298101} {:answer/id #uuid "7001b475-d922-57ee-8574-c6d799309249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{80}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298102} {:answer/id #uuid "1a197143-ec2c-5a8e-ba31-6659239a871f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298103} {:answer/id #uuid "af5d382c-98ca-54a0-9c21-06