{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298105 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "924f7e64-d426-514d-acb6-d0848553edae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298107} {:answer/id #uuid "8d494004-2ee4-546a-873f-98de77db96ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298108} {:answer/id #uuid "abcf960d-fec6-5f3f-b58b-0ff52f98ceac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298109} {:answer/id #uuid "eafbc3b6-55b1-599e-8098-4fb9da54114f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298110} {:answer/id #uuid "fa24f55b-8162-58d4-822c-7257cb574d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "924f7e64-d426-514d-acb6-d0848553edae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298107} :answer-field/id #uuid "903a53f7-4cf9-5292-a172-11b3f7eae16b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bec3fc3-9136-583c-81f6-756eaeed751b" :question/math-academy-id "q-7324" :question/problem "Express $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={30}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {30}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a45e51d-f70a-5874-b11a-869458395675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281712} {:answer/id #uuid "66d5ed59-acae-5814-88a2-c001856f340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281713} {:answer/id #uuid "9a468535-3fdd-5b63-96c6-d15132632f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281714} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8bba33-5efc-5664-abb1-64164441b219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281715} {:answer/id #uuid "e5275784-6a42-5d5e-8e9a-769842fb3714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d5ed59-acae-5814-88a2-c001856f340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281713} :answer-field/id #uuid "325ac987-ef40-57a3-8dc9-7b94c22d1867" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2efd2da-aa38-501e-9ec7-9a761ff9a60d" :question/math-academy-id "q-76641" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5ea7471-653d-593b-ab4a-dbb4fa01c82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298114} {:answer/id #uuid "4759e6f6-1b41-5d6d-8479-53f714647ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298115} {:answer/id #uuid "ea32ee4d-0d79-586d-af22-caa09e9d2fef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298116} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b19169-3466-5900-902d-ad5cc8aa1fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298117} {:answer/id #uuid "885216ae-9057-5aba-b8bb-4930d0ba5142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298118}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3b19169-3466-5900-902d-ad5cc8aa1fea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298117} :answer-field/id #uuid "7465ba39-8e25-5c6d-8bfd-1c2bd409b395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "278ccf61-185b-5071-877e-b29360496fc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-76643" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41b16cf7-9296-549b-879d-62122082de71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298121} {:answer/id #uuid "16fbb32f-674f-5776-84ce-32350